nv30: keep the index buffer's bufctx ref alive until submit

On NV40_3D, an indexed draw with a real (non-user) index buffer and
index_size > 1 programs IDXBUF_OFFSET/IDXBUF_FORMAT through PUSH_RESRC ->
PUSH_MTHD.  PUSH_MTHD does NOT relocate inline: it registers the method in
the bufctx (nouveau_bufctx_mthd -> nouveau_bufctx_refn, which puts the ref
on bctx->pending) and writes bo->offset + data using whatever offset is
known right now -- 0 for a buffer this submission has not validated yet.

libdrm's pushbuf_validate() is what turns that into a real address: it
walks bctx->pending and, for every ref with ->packet set, emits the
(method header, value) relocation pair the kernel later patches in.

nv30_draw_elements() then called PUSH_RESET(push, BUFCTX_IDXBUF) at the end
of the draw -- before the pushbuf is ever flushed.  nouveau_bufctx_reset()
does DRMLISTDELINIT on each ref in the bin, taking it straight back off
bctx->pending, so validate never sees it and the pair is never emitted.
The unrelocated value stands.

Observed on a GeForce 7 (AGP) running vbo-drawelements: the faulting push
carries 16 relocations covering every GPU address in it -- three M2MF
copy pairs, COLOR0_OFFSET, ZETA_OFFSET, FP_ACTIVE_PROGRAM, VTXBUF0 and
VTXBUF1 -- and none for IDXBUF.  IDXBUF_OFFSET reaches the GPU as a bare
0x00000100, which is not even 4K aligned and so cannot be a validated BO
address.  The engine fetches U32 indices out of unrelated VRAM, and the
garbage indices drive vertex fetches far outside the 16-byte-stride array
bound at VTXBUF0/VTXBUF1 -- DMA_VTX_PROTECTION, every time, deterministically.

BUFCTX_VTXBUF and BUFCTX_FRAGPROG are not reset in the same function, which
is exactly why they do get their relocation pairs in that same push.

Move the reset to the top of the block, so each draw still starts with a
clean bin but the ref survives to submit.

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_vbo.c	2026-09-07 10:10:59.772566855 +0000
+++ src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_vbo.c	2026-09-07 10:10:59.796689835 +0000
@@ -482,6 +482,7 @@
 
       assert(nouveau_resource_mapped_by_gpu(&res->base));
 
+      PUSH_RESET(push, BUFCTX_IDXBUF);
       BEGIN_NV04(push, NV30_3D(IDXBUF_OFFSET), 2);
       PUSH_RESRC(push, NV30_3D(IDXBUF_OFFSET), BUFCTX_IDXBUF, res, offset,
                        NOUVEAU_BO_LOW | NOUVEAU_BO_RD, 0, 0);
@@ -510,7 +511,9 @@
       }
       BEGIN_NV04(push, NV30_3D(VERTEX_BEGIN_END), 1);
       PUSH_DATA (push, NV30_3D_VERTEX_BEGIN_END_STOP);
-      PUSH_RESET(push, BUFCTX_IDXBUF);
+      /* NO reset here: the bufctx ref is what carries the deferred
+       * relocation of IDXBUF_OFFSET/FORMAT to submit time. Resetting the
+       * bin before the flush drops it, and the unrelocated offset stands. */
